From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32, bcrypt: certificate and CTL finds, physical stores, other names, UPN, invalid flags

FIXMEs and stubs in certificate handling, as documented now:

- CertFindCertificateInStore ("find type unimplemented", then nothing):
  CERT_FIND_ENHKEY_USAGE (all usages asked, or any with
  CERT_FIND_OR_ENHKEY_USAGE_FLAG; certificates good for every usage with
  CERT_FIND_OPTIONAL_ENHKEY_USAGE_FLAG; only those with
  CERT_FIND_NO_ENHKEY_USAGE_FLAG; the extension or the property alone with
  EXT_ONLY / PROP_ONLY), CERT_FIND_PROPERTY, CERT_FIND_KEY_SPEC (the
  property, else the key provider information's), CERT_FIND_SUBJECT_ATTR
  and CERT_FIND_ISSUER_ATTR, CERT_FIND_CROSS_CERT_DIST_POINTS,
  CERT_FIND_PUBKEY_MD5_HASH, CERT_FIND_SUBJECT_INFO_ACCESS,
  CERT_FIND_HASH_STR (the thumbprint in hex, spaces allowed) and
  CERT_FIND_HAS_PRIVATE_KEY; an unknown type is E_INVALIDARG.
- CertIsRDNAttrsInCertificateName: CERT_RDN_ANY_TYPE matches any value type.
- CertFindCTLInStore: CTL_FIND_USAGE (the usages, CTL_FIND_SAME_USAGE_FLAG,
  the list identifier and the signer) and CTL_FIND_SUBJECT; and
  CertFindSubjectInCTL (was "@ stub"), by identifier or by certificate
  (its hash by the CTL's subject algorithm). wincrypt.h gets
  CTL_ANY_SUBJECT_TYPE, CTL_CERT_SUBJECT_TYPE and CTL_ANY_SUBJECT_INFO.
- CRL distribution point names compare e-mail, DNS, IP address,
  registered ID and other names, not just URLs and directory names.
- CertOpenStore: physical stores (CERT_STORE_PROV_PHYSICAL_W and
  "Physical", a stub): ".Default", ".LocalMachine", ".GroupPolicy",
  ".Enterprise", and ".SmartCard" and ".UserCertificate" empty;
  CERT_STORE_PROV_PKCS12 and "PKCS12" (a PFX blob without a password);
  "File" is the file name provider (it opened a file handle store).
- Alternative names: otherName is encoded and decoded (FIXMEs that failed
  the whole name), and CertGetNameString gives CERT_NAME_UPN_TYPE, the
  szOID_NT_PRINCIPAL_NAME other name.
- CertAddCertificateLinkToStore is no longer a "semi-stub" FIXME: it adds
  a link, as documented.
- bcrypt: an unknown flag to BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider, BCryptCreateHash
  or a symmetric BCryptEncrypt/BCryptDecrypt is STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER,
  as on Windows (it was a FIXME and STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED).

Gate: test/certfind-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/certfind-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_EKU_FIND, SG_MUTANT_NO_PRIVATE_KEY_FIND (crypt32/cert.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_CTL_USAGE (crypt32/ctl.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_PHYSICAL (crypt32/store.c).
